    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d3">

                <pb facs="0072" n="2" xml:id="pg2"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.1012 Anti-War/69</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 228</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1934-03-23"
                            >March 23, 1934</date>.<lb/>[Received April 2.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my despatch No. 207 of
                    March 13, enclosing a certified copy of the Anti-War Treaty initiated by the
                    Argentine Minister for Foreign Affairs, I have the honor to enclose herewith a
                    copy and translation of a note I received today from the Minister<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d3-f1"/> asking me to obtain from my Government as soon as possible
                    the authorization to sign the document of adhesion to the Anti-War Treaty at a
                    meeting which will take place at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs in the near
                    future, at the same time as the signature of adhesion of several other
                    nations.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alexander W.
                    Weddell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
